# Build output
build/bin
/chit
/chit.exe
*.exe

# Frontend
node_modules
# written by the wails CLI to decide whether npm install needs rerunning
frontend/package.json.md5
# dist is generated, but the directory itself must exist for the go:embed in main.go
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep

# Go test and profiling artifacts
*.test
*.out
*.prof

# Internal development documentation. None of it is needed to build, run, test or
# release CH-IT: it is the roadmap, the agent handoff layer and the early planning
# notes. README.md and LICENSE are the only docs a downloader or someone building
# from source needs, and both stay tracked.
/PLAN.md
/CLAUDE.md
/CONVENTIONS.md
/prompt.md
/design.txt
/design-path.md
/idea.txt
/tools.md
/new-tools.md
/SPECS/
# Wails scaffold boilerplate describing the build directory. Nothing reads it.
build/README.md

# testdata/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is not documentation: the Go and
# TypeScript suites both read those golden files, and the tree does not pass its
# tests without them.

# Local tool and editor settings
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
